{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "The fixed shape of CLAUDE.md. Enforced by scripts/check_claude_md_size.py.",
    "",
    "Each section carries BOTH a `budget` (enforced right now) and a `target` (where it is",
    "going). This is a ratchet, the same shape .ruff-baseline uses: `budget` may only ever",
    "move DOWN, and `budget >= target` always. The hard ceilings that make the ratchet",
    "meaningful -- HARD_TOTAL_BUDGET and MAX_SECTION_BUDGET -- are CONSTANTS IN THE LINTER,",
    "not fields here, so relaxing the guard means editing code and its unit test in the same",
    "PR rather than nudging a number in a data file.",
    "",
    "Budgets are frozen at the sizes measured on main at 453b1f01 (2026-08-17). They ratchet",
    "down to `target` once the trim lands. See CONTRIBUTING.md."
  ],
